A||N||8||Fiero_Joe||need help selecting a new power plant ||||10||
Z||000000||Fiero_Joe||09-26-2000||12:46 AM||||Hi I'm not new to Fiero's but I am new to the world of mods. What I would like to do is get 300 hp out of my 85gt 4spd. I need help because I don't know if I should get a V8 (wich I don't realy want to do) or Mod my 2.8 to a 3.2... If anyone can help please let me know. I have recently spun a baring off the crank and I miss my little race car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Thanks <BR>Fiero_joe||||reg||10
Z||000001||Phil||09-26-2000||08:46 AM||||300 HP from a 2.8/3.1 and still have an engine that would last more than 100 mi and cost less than $15000  might be a bit of wishful thinking. An intercooled SC 3800 would come close or a V8 but both will be spendy. It all depends on your budget.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||09-26-2000||09:07 AM||||Just get a northstar with a turbo.  And if you REALLY want POWER, add some Nitrous to it.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000003||elfiero||09-26-2000||09:22 AM||||Really,without going to a V8(SBC)there is no<BR>CHEAP way to get 300HP reliably.Personally,<BR>I have had both SBC&3800 fieros and I would<BR>rccomend the buick every time- cheaper to<BR>put in,easier on drivetrain parts,fast enough<BR>for 99% of the drivers out there.I'll still<BR>wax you w/my TPI V8,but i'll spend more time<BR>and money keep'in it going.With the V6 you put it in and forget it.<BR> P.S.dont mess with super chargers-too <BR>expensive to buy,and the crap out too fast-<BR>if you don't belive me,check the junkyards<BR>and they will tell you most of the time the<BR>blowers take a dump around 75,000MI.<BR>P.P.S.-this stuff is all just my opinion so<BR>plllllleeaase don't flame me.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Fiero_Joe||09-26-2000||10:04 AM||||Thanks for the information. I'm still a little confused. I'm looking into V8 Archie's now. I would like to keep this little project under $5000.00. $4000.00 would be OK 5 is pushing it. Does any one think its worth my time. I found this site called Whitehorse at <BR> <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com/whitehorse/home.html#anchor-engine" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcar.com/whitehorse/home.html#anchor-engine</A>  <BR> <BR>They do Fiero Rebodies and Kit cars. They claim that they can put together a 3.1 liter GM 60ø 300hp 200tq with a 3 year unlimited mileage warranty. How does that sound?? By the way how much does the 3800 sbc go for these days(rebuilt)?||||reg||9
Z||000005||Phil||09-26-2000||10:56 AM||||Whatever you do keep in mind that emissions testing will be coming to you soon. Also 300HP for under $5k is going to be real tough.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-26-2000||07:10 PM||||I just got an email from Archie regarding the cost of installing a SBC.  $6100 for a stick or $7100 for an automatic.  This is just the labor (and his Master Kit).  This does not include the motor.  I'm guessing it would cost somewhere around 10 grand to have it done right (with a new/reman motor).  I thought it might be cheaper, but that's a little too rich for my blood.  BENGAL4 just got a S/C 3800 installed in his '86 GT.  I think he spent somewhere in the neighborhood of 8 grand.  I doubt you could do a N* any cheaper.  The big thing these days seems to be a 3.4.  They're fairly plentiful motors and can be done for less than $3000 including the motor.  If that interests you, get a hold of either Ed Parks (FieroFactory) or Bob Stieger (Twin Lakes Fiero).  Ed is in Alabama and Bob is in Illinois.  (I only assume that you're in Alabama.  Ed is in Toney.)||||reg||1
Z||000007||whamel||09-27-2000||10:56 AM||||I can break down what I've got in my V-8 conversion so far if anybody is interested.  I was thinking of keeping a 'running total' on my web site of what I put in as I go.  I'll probably do a pretty good step by step on the install as well if I am permitted to do that.  Maybe it will help some folks out.  I'll be doing pretty much all the work myself so it will be the 'bare bones' cost.  I do plan on dyno testing the whole thing when I'm done both before and after the Nitrous gets installed.<BR>I'm also planning on doing a stroked 2.8 here as well - probably do a cost breakdown of that too.  It won't be as extreme as my 350, but I would really like to get 200-230 hp out of it when I'm done.  I think that might be next years project though.<BR>Wade <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/whamel" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/whamel</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||RedOktober||09-29-2000||08:38 AM||||Joe, sorry I didn't catch a planned budget for your 300HP motor. Just remember HP=$$$-(reliability)+(reativity*2)/inginuity+BEER.<P>I just spent another $570 to upgrade my turbo and found I have a spun bearing too. 3.4 is ordered along with a new cam and misc parts and I might be under $3000( not including instalation. <P>If you are in AL, Give Ed Parks a call.Good Luck.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater)||||reg||1
